# WildcatTTS Web UI Functions - environment template
#
# IMPORTANT: the Firebase CLI DEPLOYS .env and .env.<project-id> as plaintext
# environment variables on the Cloud Run service, where anyone with
# roles/viewer can read them. Never put a credential in either file.
#
#   .env / .env.chatvibestts  -> deployed, plaintext. Non-secret config only.
#   .env.local                -> emulator only, never deployed. Local creds go here.
#   Secret Manager            -> production credentials, declared in the
#                                secretEnvironmentVariables block of firebase.json
#                                and mounted at instance startup.
#
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in.

# -- Non-secret config (safe to deploy as plaintext) --
CALLBACK_URL=https://your-domain/auth/twitch/callback
FRONTEND_URL=https://your-domain
OBS_BROWSER_BASE_URL=https://tts.wildcat.chat
TWITCH_BOT_USERNAME=WildcatTTS
TTS_BOT_URL=https://your-tts-service.run.app
ALLOWED_CHANNELS_SECRET_NAME=projects/your-project/secrets/allowed-channels/versions/latest

# -- Credentials: do NOT set these here --
# TWITCH_CLIENT_ID / TWITCH_CLIENT_SECRET / JWT_SECRET_KEY /
# WAVESPEED_API_KEY / 302_KEY come from Secret Manager in production.
# For local emulator work put the Twitch pair in functions/.env.local instead,
# and set USE_ENV_SECRETS=1 to bypass the deployed-secret code path.
